# The Verify sandbox talks to a *rootless* daemon. Without this the docker CLI
# finds /var/run/docker.sock instead, and membership of the `docker` group
# needed to reach it is root-equivalent on the host -- the posture the sandbox
# exists to avoid. Set it up via the unit shipped by `docker-rootless-extras`:
#   systemctl --user enable --now docker
#
# NOTE: this one must be a real environment variable, NOT merely a line in
# .env. pydantic-settings reads .env into the Settings object and never into
# os.environ, and `sanitized_docker_env` builds the CLI's environment from
# os.environ -- so a DOCKER_HOST living only here is silently ignored and the
# run fails against the rootful socket. Export it in your shell or your
# systemd unit:
#   export DOCKER_HOST=unix:///run/user/$(id -u)/docker.sock
